# Build context for builds run from the repository root. Today that is only
# desktop/backend.Dockerfile (see desktop/scripts/build-backend.sh), which copies `backend/` and
# `desktop/backend.spec` and nothing else.
#
# backend/Dockerfile uses ./backend as its context and is governed by backend/.dockerignore, not
# by this file.
#
# This is an allow-list: everything is excluded, then the paths a root-context Dockerfile actually
# copies are let back in. That keeps .git, deploy/, docs/, desktop/release, desktop/dist,
# desktop/node_modules, *.AppImage, any .env and any personal collection export out of the build
# context without having to enumerate them -- and a new file at the repo root is excluded by
# default. If you add a COPY of a new path to a root-context Dockerfile, allow it here.
*

!backend
!desktop/backend.spec

# Within the allowed paths, still exclude secrets, local state and test-only files.
# (A `!` rule above re-includes the whole directory, so these must come after it.)
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.env-*
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.egg-info
backend/tests
backend/.coverage
backend/.coverage.*
backend/coverage.xml
backend/htmlcov
backend/data
backend/image-cache
backend/*.csv
backend/*.dlens
backend/*.log
**/tests/fixtures/*_full.csv
**/.DS_Store
